course: dictionary
lesson: 1308
title: Cache: a hidden store
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Squirrels make a cache of nuts for winter.» Squirrels hide food to eat later, so a cache must be a hidden store of things.
explain: «Clear the cache» is a different kind of sentence. It is about a phone or computer, not a hidden box. The clue is the topic: a cache there is data kept so it can be found quickly next time. Ask yourself what would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Cache can also be a verb, so you can cache something. In «cache-cache», the French word for hide and seek, the idea of hiding is the same. In geocaching, families use GPS to find hidden boxes called caches.
fact: A cache is a hidden store of things, such as food, weapons or treasure.
fact: On a computer or phone, a cache keeps data for a while so it can be found quickly next time.
fact: To cache something means to store it, hidden or for quick use.
fact: «A cache of» means a store of something, such as «a cache of nuts».
fact: Geocaching is a game where families use GPS to find hidden boxes called caches.
exercise: «Squirrels make a cache of nuts for winter.» What is a cache here? | A warm coat for winter | *A hidden store of food | A tall tree with many leaves | A loud noise in the woods
exercise: «Clear the cache» can fix a slow phone. What is the cache? | A hidden box in a park | A kitchen cupboard for snacks | *Data kept on the phone so it can be found quickly | Lost property at the station
exercise: Which word is a verb meaning to store something hidden or for quick use? | *cache | clean | crash | cave
test: In geocaching, what is a cache? | A bag of sweets for the bus | *A hidden box that families search for with GPS | A word for a shop | A map of the stars
test: Which sentence uses cache to mean data kept on a computer? | *Clearing the cache may make the browser faster. | The squirrel hid a cache of acorns. | The cache of apples was in the barn. | The pirates buried a cache of gold.
exam: The pirates buried a cache of gold on the island. What does cache mean? | *A hidden store of treasure | A computer file that keeps web pages | A kind of small boat | A loud crash on the rocks
